WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.060
- [Instructor] In this video,
I'm going to introduce you

00:00:02.060 --> 00:00:05.370
to two units of measuring length.

00:00:05.370 --> 00:00:09.520
The first is the inch, which
you might have heard about.

00:00:09.520 --> 00:00:13.460
And you're probably thinking,
"How long is an inch?"

00:00:13.460 --> 00:00:15.750
Well, if you're familiar with a quarter,

00:00:15.750 --> 00:00:18.560
a quarter looks something like this.

00:00:18.560 --> 00:00:21.083
You see George Washington on it.

00:00:22.090 --> 00:00:24.790
A quarter is almost an inch.

00:00:24.790 --> 00:00:28.550
So an inch might be something like that.

00:00:28.550 --> 00:00:30.960
One inch.

00:00:30.960 --> 00:00:32.900
Another way to think about
it is when I'm looking

00:00:32.900 --> 00:00:35.180
at my thumb, and I'm a grown man,

00:00:35.180 --> 00:00:36.730
at least physically (chuckles),

00:00:39.800 --> 00:00:43.420
my thumb is about two inches in length.

00:00:43.420 --> 00:00:47.410
So my thumb is about two inches in length.

00:00:47.410 --> 00:00:52.410
One inch and two inches.

00:00:52.740 --> 00:00:54.640
Depending on your age,
if you're watching this

00:00:54.640 --> 00:00:56.030
and let's say you're eight years old,

00:00:56.030 --> 00:00:57.160
seven or eight years old,

00:00:57.160 --> 00:01:00.080
your thumb might be closer to an inch

00:01:00.080 --> 00:01:02.680
or maybe a little bit over an inch.

00:01:02.680 --> 00:01:04.700
Now the other unit of measurement,

00:01:04.700 --> 00:01:08.070
you can view it as a bunch
of inches put together.

00:01:08.070 --> 00:01:10.400
And if you put 12 inches together,

00:01:10.400 --> 00:01:15.400
you get what is known as a foot, a foot.

00:01:16.150 --> 00:01:19.680
Now the word foot is used for
many things in our language,

00:01:19.680 --> 00:01:22.520
including for our individual feet,

00:01:22.520 --> 00:01:25.640
or the things at the ends of our legs.

00:01:25.640 --> 00:01:27.590
And I believe, I'm not sure

00:01:27.590 --> 00:01:30.530
where the unit of measurement
of the foot came from,

00:01:30.530 --> 00:01:31.980
but they might be related

00:01:31.980 --> 00:01:36.090
because actually my foot is almost a foot.

00:01:36.090 --> 00:01:39.720
And in fact, my shoes, and I wear a size,

00:01:39.720 --> 00:01:43.340
I wear a men's size 10 1/2,

00:01:43.340 --> 00:01:45.340
my sneakers that I wear

00:01:48.279 --> 00:01:50.063
are almost exactly one foot.

00:01:51.020 --> 00:01:54.600
And you can sometimes see it
written as ft, short for foot.

00:01:54.600 --> 00:01:58.660
Now, clearly not everyone's
foot is exactly a foot

00:01:58.660 --> 00:02:01.660
'cause everyone's feet and
shoes have different lengths,

00:02:01.660 --> 00:02:05.480
but that gets you a sense
of how large a foot is.

00:02:05.480 --> 00:02:06.313
Another way to think about it,

00:02:06.313 --> 00:02:07.320
and as I just mentioned,

00:02:07.320 --> 00:02:11.440
if you put 12 inches
together, you get one foot.

00:02:11.440 --> 00:02:13.400
12 inches

00:02:16.007 --> 00:02:19.340
equals one foot.

00:02:19.340 --> 00:02:23.090
So let me give you some objects.

00:02:23.090 --> 00:02:25.560
And I want you to pause
the video and think about,

00:02:25.560 --> 00:02:27.590
would you measure them in foot or inches

00:02:27.590 --> 00:02:29.700
or whether the measurements themselves

00:02:29.700 --> 00:02:32.700
sound like measurements in feet or inches.

00:02:32.700 --> 00:02:36.350
So if I give you a piece of paper,

00:02:36.350 --> 00:02:39.820
a regular piece of paper,

00:02:39.820 --> 00:02:43.580
kind with the holes on
it and the nice lines.

00:02:43.580 --> 00:02:47.000
So a piece of paper right over here.

00:02:47.000 --> 00:02:48.380
If I were to tell you

00:02:48.380 --> 00:02:52.760
that the height of this
paper is 11 something,

00:02:52.760 --> 00:02:56.803
would that be 11 inches or 11 feet?

00:02:58.440 --> 00:03:01.610
Well, if was 11 feet, that
would be a huge piece of paper.

00:03:01.610 --> 00:03:03.980
That would be a piece
of paper taller than me.

00:03:03.980 --> 00:03:06.370
That would be more of a
carpet than a piece of paper.

00:03:06.370 --> 00:03:07.410
So a piece of paper,

00:03:07.410 --> 00:03:12.410
actually a standard piece
of paper is 11 inches tall.

00:03:12.620 --> 00:03:16.720
Now, if we were to go outside
and play a little basketball,

00:03:16.720 --> 00:03:20.840
so this is the basketball,
or that's the backboard.

00:03:20.840 --> 00:03:24.610
And then we have the hoop, the hoop,

00:03:24.610 --> 00:03:26.163
we have the net,

00:03:27.290 --> 00:03:30.380
and then we have the post holding it up.

00:03:30.380 --> 00:03:32.370
Let me draw that in a different color.

00:03:32.370 --> 00:03:33.910
So we have the post.

00:03:33.910 --> 00:03:38.910
And this is a standard NBA basketball rim.

00:03:38.960 --> 00:03:42.240
If I were to say it's 10
something off the ground,

00:03:42.240 --> 00:03:45.313
is that 10 inches or 10 feet?

00:03:46.760 --> 00:03:48.290
Well, if it was 10 inches,

00:03:48.290 --> 00:03:52.280
it would be very easy to
dunk a basketball. (chuckles)

00:03:52.280 --> 00:03:54.750
Although it might be hard to
fit the basketball in the rim

00:03:54.750 --> 00:03:58.860
because if the rim was, it
might also be very, very small.

00:03:58.860 --> 00:04:01.390
That would be more of a basketball goal

00:04:01.390 --> 00:04:04.730
for an insect of some kind or
for a very, very small mouse.

00:04:04.730 --> 00:04:06.540
For normal human beings,

00:04:06.540 --> 00:04:10.440
the standard height of a
basketball goal is 10 feet.

00:04:10.440 --> 00:04:13.390
The one that they play with in the NBA.

00:04:13.390 --> 00:04:15.420
At your school, if you're
a little bit younger,

00:04:15.420 --> 00:04:16.970
you might see a basketball goal

00:04:16.970 --> 00:04:20.030
that is six feet or
eight feet or nine feet.

00:04:20.030 --> 00:04:20.870
But the standard ones

00:04:20.870 --> 00:04:25.480
that the professionals
play with are 10 feet tall.

00:04:25.480 --> 00:04:27.010
Now let me give you some things,

00:04:27.010 --> 00:04:28.400
and I wanna decide whether it's better

00:04:28.400 --> 00:04:32.340
to measure them with feet or with inches.

00:04:32.340 --> 00:04:35.240
So let's say that I have a swimming pool,

00:04:35.240 --> 00:04:38.720
say I have a swimming
pool right over here.

00:04:38.720 --> 00:04:42.270
And that is the pool.

00:04:42.270 --> 00:04:43.630
Would it be better to measure

00:04:43.630 --> 00:04:46.880
the length of this swimming
pool in feet or in inches?

00:04:46.880 --> 00:04:48.553
Pause the video and think about that.

00:04:50.350 --> 00:04:53.920
Well, a swimming pool is fairly large.

00:04:53.920 --> 00:04:56.820
It is much larger than even a foot.

00:04:56.820 --> 00:04:58.250
So you'd think you'd want to measure it,

00:04:58.250 --> 00:05:00.010
if you had to choose
between feet and inches,

00:05:00.010 --> 00:05:01.600
you would pick feet.

00:05:01.600 --> 00:05:04.290
And so this would be a situation

00:05:04.290 --> 00:05:06.620
where that pool might be, say,

00:05:06.620 --> 00:05:10.943
75 feet long.

00:05:12.130 --> 00:05:17.120
Now, if you were measuring
the length of a mouse,

00:05:17.120 --> 00:05:18.810
this is a mouse right over here.

00:05:18.810 --> 00:05:22.790
Not my best drawing of
a mouse with its tail,

00:05:22.790 --> 00:05:24.310
its feet right over there.

00:05:24.310 --> 00:05:27.470
Would you be best off
measuring it in feet or inches?

00:05:27.470 --> 00:05:30.563
A small mouse, a mouse that
could fit in your hand.

00:05:31.670 --> 00:05:34.270
Well, that's going to be a
good bit less than a foot.

00:05:34.270 --> 00:05:36.070
So it makes sense to
measure that in inches.

00:05:36.070 --> 00:05:40.710
I've seen mice that might only
be two or three inches long.

00:05:40.710 --> 00:05:41.780
So I'll leave you there.

00:05:41.780 --> 00:05:44.750
Hopefully that gives you a
rough sense of what an inch is,

00:05:44.750 --> 00:05:47.240
what a foot is, how they're
related to each other,

00:05:47.240 --> 00:05:49.553
and when you might use one or the other.

